# Know Your Loan requires no secret to run. The FastAPI service reads only the
# CORS setting; the Streamlit app optionally reads a Gemini key.
#
# Copy to .env to set it. Leaving it unset is fine for local work: the service
# defaults to http://localhost:3000.

#   FINEPRINT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
#
# Comma-separated browser origins permitted to call the API. There is no
# frontend to configure any more; this is only needed if something else calls
# the service from a browser.

# --- Optional: the Gemini model -------------------------------------------
# Only the Streamlit app reads this, and only to phrase the panel text. With no
# key set the app still works, showing its deterministic text. Prefer pasting
# the key into .streamlit/secrets.toml (copy secrets.toml.example), which is
# what a Streamlit Community Cloud deploy uses; this env var is the local
# convenience.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY is also accepted, and takes precedence if both are set.
# Secrets win over the environment; if both [gemini] and [deepseek] are
# configured, Gemini is used.
